{
  "mitologia": {
    "intro": "Before the LDI, before Bravara, before anything had a name, there was a story the Xakaxi told their children. Almost nobody remembers it anymore.",
    "criacao": [
      "In the beginning there was nothing. Only Chaos. He wasn't good or evil: he was the push behind everything. Everything that exists, exists because Chaos moved. That's why he is the oldest of all. The Xakaxi called him Ypy, the Beginning. Today's world calls him something else: the Primordial.",
      "Chaos liked to break things. Not out of anger: because that's what he was. To him, anything left standing was wrong. At the height of his power, he made children to break things with him. The children were the elements themselves.",
      "But the children looked at each other and, instead of breaking, they built. Fire warmed, Water flowed, Earth held, Air blew, Light showed, and Darkness let things rest. What they made together was called Order.",
      "The father wouldn't have it. Everything the children raised, he tore down. So the children did what no child ever wants to do: they put everything they were into a single seal and locked their father away. The First Seal. To close it, each of them gave up a piece of themselves, and the world's magic was never that strong again.",
      "With the father locked away, Order grew. From Order came living land, animals, and people.",
      "In the pact that imprisoned the father, the six swore that nothing would ever grow too much again, because whatever grows too much becomes another Chaos. The promise came to life on its own and became the seventh god: Balance."
    ],
    "deuses_titulo": "The seven gods",
    "deuses": [
      {
        "id": "fogo",
        "nome": "Tatarã",
        "elemento": "Fire",
        "texto": "The first to move after the father. It warms, it pushes, and it can't sit still."
      },
      {
        "id": "agua",
        "nome": "Ypuã",
        "elemento": "Water",
        "texto": "It runs wherever it can. It washes, heals, and drowns, depending on the day."
      },
      {
        "id": "terra",
        "nome": "Ybyaçu",
        "elemento": "Earth",
        "texto": "The one who holds the ground. The most patient of the six."
      },
      {
        "id": "ar",
        "nome": "Ybytuã",
        "elemento": "Air",
        "texto": "Never touches the ground. Carries everything from one place to another."
      },
      {
        "id": "luz",
        "nome": "Endyara",
        "elemento": "Light",
        "texto": "The one who shows. Nobody hides from her."
      },
      {
        "id": "escuridao",
        "nome": "Pytunã",
        "elemento": "Darkness",
        "texto": "The one who lets things rest. In the statues, she always has her back to her siblings, watching something."
      },
      {
        "id": "equilibrio",
        "nome": "Ajojá",
        "elemento": "Balance · Neutral",
        "texto": "Not a child of Chaos. The pact that became a god. The keeper of the scale: it cuts down whatever grows too much, for good or for evil."
      }
    ],
    "profecia_titulo": "The Xakaxi prophecy",
    "profecia": [
      "Of all the peoples born from Order, none rose as high as the Xakaxi, the native people of Bravara. Cities in the middle of the forest, metal that held energy, all six elements in a single bloodline. And, above all, peace with Order.",
      "That was the problem. A nail that sticks out gets hammered down, even if it rose for good. In the name of Balance, the Xakaxi had to stop existing too. They had known it for a thousand years. It was in the prophecy they told their children at bedtime:"
    ],
    "verso": [
      "When the moon bleeds in front of the sun,",
      "the people who rose the highest will fall.",
      "Men will come from the sea.",
      "And what was given will be taken."
    ],
    "depois": [
      "In 1450, the moon bled. Powa, son of Pajé Yawanari, refused that fate and performed a forbidden rite. The Pajé gave his own life to seal the sacred power, and the whole people lost their memory. Powa lost his power, but not his memory. Today he goes by another name: David Kronos.",
      "At the end of his life, the Pajé came to suspect that Balance had a deeper reason for erasing the Xakaxi. He never told anyone."
    ],
    "fecho": "In the Xakaxi temple there were six statues. And, behind Darkness, a stone door with no statue at all. Nobody prayed to it. The elders said it was the door to what came before."
  },
  "localizacoes": [
    {
      "nome": "Bravara",
      "tag": "Country",
      "descricao": "The fictional nation equivalent to colonial Brazil. In 20XX, it's a land of extremes: cutting-edge technology side by side with favelas, armored wealth, and a drifting periphery. Birthplace of the Xakaxi and the stage for Kim's story."
    },
    {
      "nome": "Marelia",
      "tag": "City",
      "descricao": "The fictional São Paulo. A chaotic metropolis with corporate towers, dangerous outskirts, and the invisible presence of Yohualticit on every corner. This is where Kim sells candy on buses — and where everything begins."
    },
    {
      "nome": "Elite Academy",
      "tag": "School",
      "descricao": "Bravara's most advanced school. Augmented reality classrooms, AI assistants, facial recognition cameras. Kim and Jack study here on a 50% scholarship — secured with the help of gatekeeper Osvaldo."
    },
    {
      "nome": "Abandoned Annex",
      "tag": "Trio HQ",
      "descricao": "A deactivated building on Elite Academy's campus. Kim and Jack's secret refuge — and later the trio's headquarters. House rule: no fighting here. Anyone who risks it loses access."
    },
    {
      "nome": "Risca a Faca",
      "tag": "Nightclub",
      "descricao": "A nightclub in one of Marelia's most degraded areas. Kim and Jack work night security here. Violent environment, R$300 a night — negotiated up from R$200 by Jack. The 'Big Man' owns the place."
    },
    {
      "nome": "Abandoned Parking Lot",
      "tag": "Hangout",
      "descricao": "A decommissioned police station turned parking lot, full of rusted impounded cars. Where the trio drinks, talks, and plans. No hierarchy, no cameras. Their confessional booth."
    },
    {
      "nome": "Davoss",
      "tag": "Private Island",
      "descricao": "An island in the South Pacific. David Kronos's private property. Home of the LDI World Tournament — held every 4 years with the top 128 players on Earth. A place where prestige and threat coexist."
    },
    {
      "nome": "Azuma",
      "tag": "Nation",
      "descricao": "The fictional Japan of the ISA universe. Home of Shuntaro Chirasu, ranked 998th worldwide in the SDR. He traveled 9 hours to personally challenge Kim at Elite Academy."
    }
  ],
  "timeline": [
    {
      "ano": "1450",
      "titulo": "Xakaxi at Peak",
      "texto": "The Xakaxi tribe thrives: carbon fiber, robotic agriculture, Xakaxium metal, six elements mastered. Then Powa — the shaman's son — performs a forbidden ritual. Pajé Yawanari sacrifices his own body to seal the sacred power. The tribe's technological memory is erased."
    },
    {
      "ano": "1500",
      "titulo": "Feudal Invasion",
      "texto": "Feudal invaders arrive in Bravara. The Xakaxi, stripped of spiritual protection and technological memory, are conquered. Yawanari watches helplessly as a guardian spirit."
    },
    {
      "ano": "1637",
      "titulo": "Colonial Massacre",
      "texto": "Conquistadors massacre and enslave the native populations of Bravara. Yawanari witnesses every death, trapped in the spirit realm."
    },
    {
      "ano": "1789",
      "titulo": "Durkria Revolt",
      "texto": "Rebellion in Bravara — met with mass public executions. More blood for the spirit who cannot intervene."
    },
    {
      "ano": "1905",
      "titulo": "First Global War",
      "texto": "The first world-scale conflict. Yawanari watches humanity destroy itself for the first time at industrial scale."
    },
    {
      "ano": "1939",
      "titulo": "Second Global War",
      "texto": "Concentration camps. Bombs. Systematic destruction. The guardian spirit witnesses human cruelty reach new heights."
    },
    {
      "ano": "2001",
      "titulo": "Global Attacks",
      "texto": "Towers fall. The world's relationship with security and paranoia changes forever. Yawanari no longer understands the species he swore to guard."
    },
    {
      "ano": "2020",
      "titulo": "The Great Void",
      "texto": "Global pandemic reshapes society. Isolation, mass death, economic collapse. The world that emerges is different — more digital, more unequal."
    },
    {
      "ano": "2022",
      "titulo": "LDI Is Born",
      "texto": "Yohualticit creates LDI. Within one year, it outsells every console ever released. Three billion people. Real pain. Global rankings. A new kind of sport is born."
    },
    {
      "ano": "2024",
      "titulo": "The PowWow Era",
      "texto": "Short-video platforms arrive and dominate the world. PowWow explodes. Yawanari, condemned to watch humanity, discovers 15-second videos. He finally loses his mind completely."
    },
    {
      "ano": "20XX",
      "titulo": "The Story Begins",
      "texto": "Kim is 17, sells candy on buses, and studies at Elite Academy on a 50% scholarship. A bet with Thunderbolt throws him into LDI. The Sangue Primordial wakes up. David Kronos notices. Nothing is ever the same."
    }
  ],
  "modos_combate": [
    {
      "nome": "Free Hands",
      "icone": "✊",
      "descricao": "Pure combat without weapons. Consumes the least energy while granting superhuman speed and strength. Ideal for reading your opponent before committing resources. Kim uses it as his base before calling the Xakixi."
    },
    {
      "nome": "Weapon Mode",
      "icone": "⚔️",
      "descricao": "Player's personal weapon in action. Acquired through random loot packages or rare spontaneous manifestation (like Kim's Xakixi). Each weapon has Normal Mode and Xamã Mode — Xamã is far more powerful but drains energy fast."
    },
    {
      "nome": "Power Mode",
      "icone": "⚡",
      "descricao": "Uses the player's elemental affinity. Three durations: Instant (low cost), Medium, and Long (high power, high cost — player is vulnerable during charging). Max 4 active powers per battle. New powers can emerge spontaneously mid-fight."
    }
  ],
